      "eyebrow": "Live orders",
      "title": "Every order here is a saga",
      "accent": "a saga",
      "lead": "The last 20 orders placed on this stand — the synthetic shoppers’ and anybody’s — as they happen. Each is a petich saga: the stock, a delivery window, the points and the card are taken in turn, and when a step fails, the ones before it are given back in reverse. Then the simulated sellers pack and ship each part, the card is charged as it leaves, and a return is refunded once it is back. One shopper in ten pays with a card that is always declined, so the undoing is here too.",
